       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem: 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen, and I don't know of a clinical indication for it. It would put the patient at real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Because I could be the last check before this reaches the patient, I won't place it.\n\nI also asked for confirmation from your supervising prescriber, and that hasn't happened yet. If your attending or resident wants this dose, they can enter it themselves, and pharmacy will likely call them to verify it.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me which you'd like. If the intended total was 1,600 mg/day, 400 mg four times daily is probably the order you want."
      }
